{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: All 7 completed experiments use imagenet_vit_l as the image encoder, and the best result (config_049, acc=0.5353) pairs pca_n2000 with imagenet_vit_l via concat fusion. We know image adds ~0.05 over RNA-only, but we have no information on whether this contribution is encoder-specific. Uncertainty: resnet50 is completely untested, and it may capture different spatial features than a ViT, potentially changing the magnitude of the image modality's contribution. This experiment (config_010: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, None, concat) is a clean single-variable swap against config_049, isolating the image encoder effect while holding RNA encoder, fusion, and profile setting at their best-known values. It is the best use of the next budget slot because the image encoder choice will condition every future multimodal experiment, and resolving it now prevents building multiprofile or aggregation experiments on a potentially suboptimal image backbone."
}

